  "|Drawings by the owner of a sole trader are:|An expense in the profit and loss account|Deducted from capital in the balance sheet|Added to capital|Credited to the cash account only": "final-accounts",
  "|Which of the following is an intangible fixed asset?|Machinery|Land and buildings|Goodwill and patents|Motor vehicles": "depreciation-assets",
  "|A credit balance in the suspense account indicates:|Debit entries exceed credit entries in the trial balance|Credit entries exceed debit entries in the trial balance|All accounts are balanced|No errors exist in the books": "trial-balance-errors",
  "|Under the FIFO (First In, First Out) method of stock valuation:|The most recently purchased stock is assumed to be sold first|The oldest stock is assumed to be issued/sold first|All stock is valued at average cost|The highest-cost stock is sold first": "stock-valuation",
  "|Which of the following would NOT cause a trial balance to disagree?|Posting ₦500 to the wrong side of an account|Omitting a transaction from the books entirely|Transposing figures (e.g., writing ₦369 as ₦396)|Making an arithmetical error in a ledger balance": "trial-balance-errors",
  "|The return on capital employed (ROCE) ratio measures:|How efficiently a company uses its capital to generate profit|The proportion of profits paid as dividends|The liquidity of the business|The debt-to-equity ratio": "interpretation",
  "|Which of the following is a source document for accounting entries?|Trial balance|Balance sheet|Invoice|Profit and loss account": "source-documents",
  "|The journal (journal proper) is used to:|Record only cash transactions|Record transactions that do not fit into any specialised book — mainly adjusting entries, opening entries, corrections of errors|Summarise all ledger account balances|Record bank transactions exclusively": "source-documents",
  "|Goodwill in a partnership arises when:|The business makes large profits every year|A new partner joins or an old partner retires, requiring the existing goodwill to be valued and shared between partners|The firm buys expensive machinery|The business pays all its debts": "partnership",
  "|Which accounting convention states that assets should be recorded at their original purchase price?|Consistency|Materiality|Historical cost convention|Realisation": "nature-concepts",
