  "|When goods are returned by a customer, the entry is:|Dr Sales Returns / Cr Debtors|Dr Debtors / Cr Sales Returns|Dr Purchases / Cr Sales|Dr Cash / Cr Debtors": "double-entry",
  "|Which of the following is a feature of a limited liability company?|The owners are personally liable for all debts|The company is not a separate legal entity|Shareholders' liability is limited to the amount unpaid on their shares|The company cannot sue or be sued": "companies",
  "|In accounting, 'prepayments' are:|Expenses incurred but not yet paid|Expenses paid in advance for goods or services not yet received|Income earned but not yet received|Amounts owed to suppliers": "final-accounts",
  "|The average cost of stock method (AVCO) values closing stock at:|The cost of the oldest items in stock|The cost of the most recent items|The weighted average cost of all units purchased during the period|The market value of stock": "stock-valuation",
  "|Which of the following is an example of a non-current (fixed) liability?|Bank overdraft|Trade creditors|Long-term bank loan repayable in 7 years|Accrued expenses": "final-accounts",
  "|The purpose of depreciation is to:|Reduce the market value of an asset|Allocate the cost of a tangible fixed asset over its useful economic life, matching cost with revenue generated|Increase profits shown in the accounts|Replace the asset at the end of its life": "depreciation-assets",
  "|An imprest system of petty cash means:|Petty cash is held in coins only|The petty cash balance is restored to a fixed amount at the start of each period by reimbursing the total spent|Petty cash can be spent on any amount|Petty cash replaces the main cash book": "cash-book",
  "|Which of the following ratios measures a business's ability to pay its short-term debts?|Return on capital employed|Debt/equity ratio|Current ratio (Current Assets / Current Liabilities)|Net profit margin": "interpretation",
  "|In accounting, the matching concept means:|Assets must always equal liabilities|Revenue earned in a period should be matched with the expenses incurred to generate that revenue in the same period|All income must be received in cash|Capital equals profits": "nature-concepts",
  "|Which of the following errors would be revealed by a trial balance?|Error of omission|Error of commission|Error of principle|Arithmetic error causing unequal debit and credit totals": "trial-balance-errors",
  "|The concept of 'going concern' in accounting assumes:|The business will close at year end|The business will continue to operate for the foreseeable future, justifying long-term asset valuation|All debts will be paid immediately|Assets will be sold at market value": "nature-concepts",
  "|In a sole trader's accounts, the owner's drawings are:|Added to profit in the profit and loss account|Deducted from capital in the balance sheet|Shown as an expense in the trading account|Treated as a liability": "final-accounts",
